        "r": 411.66134062509974,
        "b": 678.3472949280329
      },
      "content": "The conventions listed in Table 1-1 are used throughout this manual."
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "id": "tbl_0006",
      "reading_order": 43,
      "section": "1.2 CONVENTIONS",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 70.56652069091797,
        "t": 660.5508422851562,
        "r": 504.9085693359375,
        "b": 504.0980529785156
      },
      "markdown": "| Table 1-1. Conventions   | Table 1-1. Conventions                                | Table 1-1. Conventions                                                 |\n|--------------------------|-------------------------------------------------------|------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Convention               | Application                                           | Example                                                                |\n| Italic                   | Reference to a section, figure, table, or publication | (see Section 6.1)                                                      |\n| [ALL CAPS]               | In-text references to keys and touchswitches          | [START]                                                                |\n| ALL CAPS                 | Screen displays                                       | CASSETTE TEST IN PROGRESS                                              |\n| Bold                     | Emphasis                                              | CAUTION: Use proper ESD grounding techniques when handling components. |"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0035",
      "reading_order": 44,
      "section": "1.2 CONVENTIONS",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 71.99880479880002,
        "t": 484.562499316,
        "r": 503.9565700909003,
        "b": 463.6672473860328
      },
      "content": "Throughout this manual, warnings, cautions, and notes are used to emphasize important information as follows:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0036",
      "reading_order": 45,
      "section": "1.2 CONVENTIONS",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 91.8,
        "t": 432.98365,
        "r": 149.15732399999996,
        "b": 422.82715
      },
      "content": "WARNING:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0037",
      "reading_order": 46,
      "section": "1.2 CONVENTIONS",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 167.16,
        "t": 432.91126718,
        "r": 486.8185529420011,
        "b": 403.71847787
      },
      "content": "A WARNING CONTAINS SPECIAL SAFETY EMPHASIS AND MUST BE OBSERVED AT ALL TIMES. FAILURE TO OBSERVE A WARNING MAY RESULT IN PATIENT INJURY AND BE LIFE-THREATENING."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0038",
      "reading_order": 47,
      "section": "1.2 CONVENTIONS",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 71.99880479880002,
        "t": 374.930677244,
        "r": 504.0231029576997,
        "b": 341.73966422908546
      },
      "content": "CAUTION: A  CAUTION  usually  appears  in  front  of  a  procedure  or  statement. It contains information that could prevent hardware failure, irreversible damage to equipment, or loss of data."
    },
    {
